    "problemStatement": "This problem has subtasks.\n\nGiven an array AAA, you can perform the following operation on it:\n\n\nChoose three indices i,j,ki, j, ki,j,k such that 1≤i&lt;j&lt;k≤∣A∣1 \\leq i \\lt j \\lt k \\leq |A|1≤i&lt;j&lt;k≤∣A∣ and Ai&lt;Aj&lt;AkA_i \\lt A_j \\lt A_kAi​&lt;Aj​&lt;Ak​, and delete AjA_jAj​.\n\nThat is, choose an increasing subsequence of length 333 in AAA and delete its middle element.\n\n∣A∣|A|∣A∣ denotes the length of AAA, which reduces by 111 after the operation is performed.\nFor example, if A=[2,5,3,1,4]A = [2, 5, 3, 1, 4]A=[2,5,3,1,4], you can choose i=1,j=3,k=5i = 1, j = 3, k = 5i=1,j=3,k=5 and delete the middle element, which results in A=[2,5,1,4]A = [2, 5, 1, 4]A=[2,5,1,4].\n\nDefine f(A)f(A)f(A) to be the minimum possible sum of AAA after performing several such operations on it.\n\nYou are given an array PPP of length NNN containing elements between 000 and NNN.\n\nIt is guaranteed that all the non-zero elements of PPP are distinct.\n\nFind the sum of f(Q)f(Q)f(Q) across all permutations QQQ that can be obtained by filling in the zeros of PPP.\n\nFormally, find the sum of f(Q)f(Q)f(Q) across all arrays QQQ of length NNN such that:\n\n\nQQQ contains every integer from 111 to NNN exactly once each.\nIf Pi&gt;0P_i \\gt 0Pi​&gt;0, then Pi=QiP_i = Q_iPi​=Qi​.\nThe answer can be large, so compute it modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the length of array PPP.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers P1,P2,…,PNP_1, P_2, \\ldots, P_NP1​,P2​,…,PN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the sum of f(Q)f(Q)f(Q) across all valid arrays QQQ, modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
